# Gloom Ripper {3}{B}{B} 4/4: "When this creature enters, target creature you control gets +X/+0 until end of turn and up to one target
# creature an opponent controls gets -0/-X until end of turn, where X is the number of Elves you control plus the number of Elf cards in
# your graveyard" (CR 611.2a, 608.2h). In turn 3 Bot1's Scarblade Scout (an Elf Scout) mills Llanowar Elves and an Island, then Gloom
# Ripper (an Elf too) enters: X is 2 Elves it controls + 1 Elf card in its graveyard = 3, so Gloom Ripper becomes 7/4 and Bot2's Wall
# of Earth (0/6) becomes 0/3. The two numbers differ and are not 2 and 2, so adding them is told from multiplying. Four Moxen and
# Black Lotus pay for both in turn 3.

